# Computer Use is hands, not a second brain

You (the parent) write the `computerUse` Task prompt. The clicker starts
with a clean context: no parent conversation, and no automatic load of
`AGENTS.md`, `.cursor/rules`, or `knowledge/*`. Cursor's unpublished
computer-use prompt is fixed. Bound the job so conservative observation
cannot become an open-ended scroll.

Before any `computerUse` spawn:

1. Resolve facts in the parent. Compile an action sheet of final actions
   in page order. Do not ask the clicker to rediscover the form.
2. Run `python3 scripts/compile_cu_task.py compile <sheet.yaml>`.
   If you write a Task by hand, run `lint` on it. Hits mean do not send.
3. One mode per spawn: execute, verify, repair, or submit. Do not combine
   execute with a full-form audit.

Forbidden in the Task: verify-each-field, report every untouched widget,
whole-form screenshot tours, fitting distant facts into one viewport,
unbounded retries, Ctrl+F, Run Autofill Again, Generate with AI.

After mutations: wait for settle, capture the minimum evidence, stop.
A truncated textarea is expected. Distant facts get two screenshots.

Searchable dropdowns: click the option (highlight is not a commit), Tab
off, one read-back, one alternate commit, then unresolved. Do not loop.

Submit only when the compiled sheet has `mode: submit` and
`submit_permitted: true` under an open gate of
`docs/policy/SUBMIT_ROLLOUT.md`, and then exactly once.

Canonical contract: `docs/automation/COMPUTER_USE_PROMPT.md`.
Leftover Why-us paste is still one execute/paste spawn.
